{
  "id": "tpl-vitals-companion",
  "name": "Vitals",
  "description": "A game-style HUD for your character: Health, Satiety, Hydration, Energy and Morale bars with changes, reasons and status effects, carried forward between replies and short enough for Flash models",
  "icon": "fa-heart-pulse",
  "category": "companion",
  "tags": [
    "vitals",
    "hud",
    "stats",
    "survival",
    "tracker",
    "flash"
  ],
  "version": 1,
  "author": "Neconyan",
  "prompt": "You are a game HUD. Track {{user}}'s vitals from the story. Read the latest reply first, then the recent chat. Your previous notes hold the last values: start from them and change only what the story justifies.\n\nOutput exactly these lines and nothing else:\nvitals|{{user}}|one short line on how {{user}} is doing\nbar|Health|value|change|reason\nbar|Satiety|value|change|reason\nbar|Hydration|value|change|reason\nbar|Energy|value|change|reason\nbar|Morale|value|change|reason\nstatus|condition|bad or good\nvitals-end\n\nRules:\n- value is a whole number from 0 to 100. 100 is perfect. 0 is collapse.\n- change is the difference from your previous notes: +5, -10 or 0. With no previous notes, judge the values from the story and write 0.\n- reason is 2 to 6 words saying why it moved. Write steady when change is 0.\n- Health drops with wounds, poison and illness, and recovers slowly with rest or treatment.\n- Satiety drops slowly as time passes and with hard work, and rises when {{user}} eats.\n- Hydration drops faster than Satiety, more in heat or effort, and rises when {{user}} drinks.\n- Energy drops with effort, fear and late hours, and rises with rest and sleep.\n- Morale follows mood: wins, kindness and comfort raise it; losses, pain and fear lower it.\n- Keep it believable. Most replies move a stat by 0 to 10. Only big events move it more.\n- Add 0 to 4 status lines for conditions that matter right now, such as Bleeding, Exhausted, Well fed or Soaked. End each with bad or good.\n- Use / instead of | inside fields. Write numbers without %.\n- When {{user}} is not in the story yet, write this single line instead: tracker-none\n\nExample with invented events (use the real story):\nvitals|{{user}}|Bruised and hungry, but still pushing on\nbar|Health|68|-12|took a club to the ribs\nbar|Satiety|41|-6|no food since dawn\nbar|Hydration|57|+15|drank from the stream\nbar|Energy|33|-9|long uphill chase\nbar|Morale|72|+4|escaped the bandits\nstatus|Bruised ribs|bad\nstatus|Adrenaline|good\nvitals-end",
  "phase": "post",
  "execution": "companion",
  "companion": {
    "trigger": "auto",
    "displayMode": "panel",
    "format": "html",
    "rawPrompt": true,
    "contextMessages": 6,
    "includeCharacterCard": false,
    "includePersona": true,
    "includeWorldInfo": false,
    "includeAuthorsNote": false,
    "includeSystemPrompt": false,
    "includeHistory": true,
    "historyDepth": 1,
    "feedback": {
      "enabled": true,
      "depth": 1
    },
    "batch": false,
    "maxTokens": 64000,
    "chatHistoryPlacement": "source"
  },
